---
import App from "../layouts/App.astro";
import CopyBox from "../components/CopyBox.astro";

// The MCP server is live at mcp.launchwright.app. The status card is filled in from /api/me.
const url = "https://mcp.launchwright.app/mcp";
const tools = [
  { id: "claude", label: "Claude Code", where: "In your project folder, in the terminal:", text: `claude mcp add --transport http launchwright ${url}` },
  { id: "cursor", label: "Cursor", where: "Add this to .cursor/mcp.json in your project:", text: `{ "mcpServers": { "launchwright": { "url": "${url}" } } }` },
  { id: "codex", label: "Codex", where: "Add this to ~/.codex/config.toml:", text: `[mcp_servers.launchwright] url = "${url}"` },
];
const steps = [
  { t: "Add Launchwright to your AI tool", d: "One line. Pick your tool below." },
  { t: "Sign in when it asks", d: "A browser window opens. Sign in with GitHub." },
  { t: "Take the tour", d: "Start the lesson-start prompt with your repo (owner/name). It shows you everything below on your own app." },
];
---
<App title="Connect AI tool" page="connect">
  <div class="flex flex-col gap-4">
    <div>
      <p class="label">Connect AI tool</p>
      <h1 class="text-[clamp(1.5rem,2.2vw,1.875rem)] font-bold leading-tight tracking-[-0.02em]">Keep using the AI tool you have</h1>
    </div>

    <ol class="grid grid-cols-1 gap-3 @3xl:grid-cols-3">
      {steps.map((s, i) => (
        <li class="card rounded-xl flex flex-col gap-1.5 p-4">
          <span class="grid size-9 place-items-center rounded-full bg-ink text-[14px] font-semibold text-on-ink">{i + 1}</span>
          <p class="text-base font-semibold">{s.t}</p>
          <p class="text-muted">{s.d}</p>
        </li>
      ))}
    </ol>

    <div class="card rounded-xl p-0">
      <div role="tablist" aria-label="AI tool" data-tabs class="tabs px-4 pt-4">
        {tools.map((t, i) => (
          <button type="button" role="tab" id={`tab-${t.id}`} aria-controls={`panel-${t.id}`} aria-selected={i === 0 ? "true" : "false"} class="tab">{t.label}</button>
        ))}
      </div>
      {tools.map((t) => (
        <div id={`panel-${t.id}`} role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby={`tab-${t.id}`} class="flex flex-col gap-4 p-4">
          <CopyBox label={t.where} text={t.text} />
          <p class="text-[14px] text-muted">Then restart {t.label}. You'll see <code>launchwright</code> in its list of tools.</p>
        </div>
      ))}
    </div>

    <div class="card rounded-xl flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-4 p-4">
      <div>
        <p class="text-base font-semibold"><span data-unless="mcp.connected">Waiting for your first connection</span><span hidden data-if="mcp.connected">Your AI tool is connected</span></p>
        <p class="text-muted"><span data-unless="mcp.connected">Once your AI tool makes its first launchwright call, it shows up here (refresh the page).</span><span hidden data-if="mcp.connected" data-bind="mcp.lastSeen"></span></p>
      </div>
      <span class="tag tag-line" data-class="tag-ok:mcp.connected;tag-line:mcp.notConnected"><span class="size-2 rounded-full bg-muted" data-class="bg-ok:mcp.connected" aria-hidden="true"></span><span data-bind="mcp.label">Not connected yet</span></span>
    </div>

    <div class="card rounded-xl flex flex-col gap-2 p-4">
      <p class="text-base font-semibold">Then connect your accounts</p>
      <p class="text-muted">Deploys, secrets and databases need your own Cloudflare account and a Neon or Supabase database (free tiers are enough). Your AI tool never sees their keys.</p>
      <a class="btn btn-sm self-start" href="/security#connect-cloudflare">Connect accounts</a>
    </div>

    <div class="card rounded-xl flex flex-col gap-2 p-4">
      <p class="text-base font-semibold">What your AI tool can do with launchwright</p>
      <ul class="grid grid-cols-1 gap-x-6 gap-y-1 text-[14px] @2xl:grid-cols-2">
        <li><code>project_status</code> <span class="text-muted">what your app is built with, and the next step</span></li>
        <li><code>check_readiness</code> <span class="text-muted">the 8 production readiness checks</span></li>
        <li><code>check_env</code> <span class="text-muted">settings the code needs vs. what production has</span></li>
        <li><code>set_secret</code> <span class="text-muted">you type the value here; the AI only knows the name</span></li>
        <li><code>connect_database</code> <span class="text-muted">Neon or Supabase, connection string never shown</span></li>
        <li><code>setup_ci</code> <span class="text-muted">a pull request with CI, previews, deploys and a pre-commit secret scan</span></li>
        <li><code>deploy</code> <span class="text-muted">previews now; production after you approve</span></li>
        <li><code>get_logs</code> <span class="text-muted">CI and Worker logs, secrets hidden</span></li>
        <li><code>explain_error</code> <span class="text-muted">an error in plain words, and the smallest fix</span></li>
        <li><code>review_pr</code> <span class="text-muted">review a pull request with you, risky parts first</span></li>
      </ul>
      <p class="text-[14px] text-muted">Guided lessons are MCP prompts: start with <code>lesson-start</code>, then look for <code>lesson-deploy</code>, <code>lesson-secrets</code>, <code>lesson-debug</code>, <code>lesson-practice</code> and friends in your tool's prompt or slash-command list.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="card rounded-xl flex flex-col gap-3 p-4" id="tools-and-prompts">
      <p class="text-base font-semibold">Two ways to use launchwright</p>
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 gap-4 @2xl:grid-cols-2">
        <div class="flex flex-col gap-1.5">
          <p class="font-semibold">Tools: ask in plain words</p>
          <p class="text-[14px] text-muted">Tell your AI tool what you want and name your repo. It picks the tool, does the work, and explains the lesson.</p>
          <ul class="flex flex-col gap-1 text-[14px]">
            <li><code>Use launchwright to check my project octocat/hello-world</code></li>
            <li><code>Use launchwright to review PR #3 on octocat/hello-world</code></li>
            <li><code>Use launchwright to show the latest CI error on octocat/hello-world</code></li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="flex flex-col gap-1.5">
          <p class="font-semibold">Prompts: start a guided lesson</p>
          <p class="text-[14px] text-muted">Pick a lesson from your tool's slash-command or prompt menu. Its one argument is your repo as <code>owner/name</code>, not a tool or lesson name.</p>
          <ul class="flex flex-col gap-1 text-[14px]">
            <li><span class="text-muted">Claude Code:</span> <code>/launchwright:lesson-start octocat/hello-world</code></li>
            <li><span class="text-muted">Cursor, Codex and others:</span> <span class="text-muted">find <code>lesson-start</code> in the prompt menu and enter your repo</span></li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="text-[14px] text-muted">Either way, your AI tool never sees your secrets, production deploys wait for your approval here, and launchwright only opens pull requests: you review and merge them.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</App>
